<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">François Duvalier</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1907–1971</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Papa Doc</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">François Duvalier, known as Papa Doc, was a Haitian physician elected president in 1957 who declared himself president for life in 1964. He ruled through terror, using the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tonton-macoute">Tonton Macoute</a> militia to kill and intimidate opponents, and drew on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haitian-vodou">Vodou</a> imagery to support his power. Thousands were killed and many educated Haitians emigrated. His son Jean-Claude succeeded him in 1971.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francois-duvalier.jpg" alt="François Duvalier" width="320" height="376" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fran%C3%A7ois_Duvalier_Presidential_Portrait_(1957).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
